cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Verification scripts for "The resource cost of magic in a code block"
message: >-
  If you use these scripts, please cite the paper they accompany.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Shen
    given-names: Jiachen
    affiliation: >-
      Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering,
      University of Houston
    email: jshen28@cougarnet.uh.edu
  - family-names: Zhong
    given-names: Hui
    affiliation: >-
      Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering,
      University of Houston
    email: hzhongzg@gmail.com
license: MIT
repository-code: >-
  https://github.com/Mercury0828/magic-cultivation-artifact
abstract: >-
  Scripts that check the numerical statements of the paper "The resource cost of
  magic in a code block": the one-qubit norm constants and the normalisation
  lemma, the two combinatorial facts about the rotated surface code behind the
  standard-round proposition, the accepted effect of the split-readout family,
  and the closed forms and asymptotics of the weak-string protocol.
keywords:
  - quantum error correction
  - surface code
  - resource theory of magic
  - magic state cultivation
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: The resource cost of magic in a code block
  authors:
